From d1bae471f7b068f015c3ef47f9a3aa687214d8c8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: MasherDon <62326358+MasherDon@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 14:56:54 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 37/92] moe-stream : the host tier in size classes (SiegeLadder
 M3), runahead's pass skips its pairs off the card, the drop rule's inputs in
 one tensor, and the pass's attention by part of the heads (G21, a
 measurement) - M3: a pool per slab length (gate / up 3 041 280 B in 3 051
 520-byte slots, down 3 870 720 B in 3 878 912), each with its own CLOCK hand
 and sized by the slabs of its class in the model, slots numbered across the
 pools so a slot index means to every caller what it did; classes whose slots
 differ by less than 1/16 share a pool. 4 948 experts at 46 GiB instead of 4
 244: drive reads -14.4%, L2 70.7 -> 74.8%, decode +2.2% (SiegeLadder runs.md
 4.57 / 4.59, ABBA blocks; text = trace, the pools evict 2.07 times per slot
 both); LLAMA_MOE_STREAM_L2_CLASSES=0 = one pool. A pinned allocation that
 comes back as an ordinary CPU buffer (the CUDA host buffer type falls back to
 one quietly) no longer counts as the pinned tier - it is neither page-locked
 nor aligned for direct I/O - and the one-pool slot is rounded up to 4096 as
 well. LLAMA_MOE_STREAM_RA_SKIP (default on, 0 = before): runahead's first
 half gives the pass's pairs off the card the skip id instead of a borrowed
 resident slot, and the pass's down GEMM zeroes their rows (op_params[2] = 1)
 - the zeros weight 0 made, so the same guess; only where the pass ends in
 that mul_mat_id on a CUDA cache. Speed 0% with the order controlled (the pass
 keeps 87.7% of its pairs; an early +1.6% was the position in the pair).
 LLAMA_MOE_STREAM_DROP_PACK (default on, 0 = apart): the drop rule's expert
 ids ride as floats (exact below 2^24) next to the routing weights in one F32
 tensor [k, 2*n_tokens], one card input of the remap's CPU split instead of
 two, unpacked by remap_v / remap_issue - the deterministic DROP_VRAM_ONLY=3
 gives PPL, KL, max KLD, top-1 and 92 633 drops identical to the build before
 it, and no measurable gain (14.17 vs 14.19 tok/s: the second synchronize
 waits for an idle card). LLAMA_MOE_STREAM_RA_GROUPS=g (+ _SCALE=1, off by
 default): the pass's next-layer attention on the heads of the first g of the
 8 output groups, through views of the same weights (wq_b rows, attn_sinks,
 wo_a slices, a strided view of wo_b's columns) - half the groups save 3.1 ms
 of GEMV per token but cut the guess's recall 92 -> 76% with 7x the false
 stages, -5.5% (runs.md 4.58)

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
